    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d352-a3">

                <pb facs="0548" n="476" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg476"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Appendix 2 to inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Williams to
                        Messrs. Fogarty &amp; Johnson and
                        others.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate-General</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Havana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-05-23"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 23,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: Replying to your communication of the
                    12th instant, I beg to say that the course of procedure prescribed to this
                    consulate-general prevents it, in the absence of instructions from the
                    Department of State at Washington, from initiating negotiations with the
                    governor-general of the island for the introduction of live fish from the coast
                    of Florida for sale in the markets of Havana.</p>
                <pb facs="0549" n="477" xml:id="pg477"/>
                <p>However, with the view of subserving your interests, I send by this week’s mail a
                    translated copy of your communication to the Department, which I respectfully
                    submit for its action.</p>
                <p>I remain, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>R. O. WILLIAMS,<lb/><lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Vice-Consul-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
